  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscCare 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "During a community advisory board meeting, you share that your mother\u2019s
    treatment caused severe nerve pain that made daily tasks difficult. The research
    team uses this feedback to explore new treatments that might avoid this side
    effect.\n\n<b>Why is it important for research teams to hear from caregivers?</b>"
  explanation: Caregivers see firsthand how cancer and its treatments affect daily
    life. Their experiences help scientists focus early research on what truly matters
    to patients and families. By including these perspectives from the start, researchers
    can design treatments that are not only effective, but also easier, safer, and
    more supportive for those living with cancer.
  correctAnswer: Because caregivers can share what lesser-known treatment side effects
    and challenges affect daily life most.
  incorrectAnswer1: Because caregivers can help determine which treatments move forward
    to clinical trials.
  incorrectAnswer2: Because caregivers know how to design and test new treatments
    in the lab.
  incorrectAnswer3: "Because caregivers can help researchers write medical regulations
    for new treatments once they\u2019ve been approved."
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
